From 569e358932f24753418e592f5ff7eeca803909e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Witt <rzwitt@googlemail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 15:55:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make saved state, lock times and weekly records visible
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Picks page
- Counter now says what is true: "7 / 10 saved · 3 to go", "10 / 10 saved ✓",
  "saving…", or a red "NOT saved, check your connection" when the Firebase
  write fails (it used to fall back to localStorage silently).
- "Submit Picks" renamed "Review Picks" and enabled from the first pick; it
  never wrote anything, so the overlay now reads back what is saved with each
  pick's kickoff and lock state, sorted by kickoff.
- New line under the counter: "Your first pick locks Thu 5:15 PM · in 2d 4h",
  refreshed every minute; turns red inside three hours.
- Header and name modal show the loaded week/season instead of hardcoded
  "Week 1".
- "Playing as … (switch)" becomes "Picking as … Not you?" with a readable link.
- Removed three dead copies of the avatar block that were nested inside
  <script src> tags (browsers ignore them; the real one is in the main script).

Leaderboard
- Weekly table gains W-L-P and Left (picks on games not yet scored) columns.
- Status line under the weekly header: "38 of 102 games scored · 64 still to
  play or score · 120 picks still live … As of Sun 4:25 PM", or "Final".
- Week picker lists any week with games, so the current week appears before
  its first game is scored instead of the section vanishing.
- Header week reads the loaded week, not just the last scored one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
